{"type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"name": "South Bristol Liveable Neighbourhoods study area", "note": "Digitised from Bristol City Council's published study-area map (SBLN_Map.jpg on the 'About the South Bristol Liveable Neighbourhoods' page), georeferenced to about 2.5m per pixel by fitting the ward boundaries drawn on it to Open Data Bristol's Wards layer. Each stretch then takes its geometry from the best available source: where the study-area line follows a ward boundary (about 40% of its length \u2014 the whole south-west edge around Ashton Vale, the southern edge along the Bedminster/Bishopsworth boundary, and the eastern edge past Perrett's Park) the ward geometry is used directly; where it follows a road or railway (about 30% \u2014 Coronation Road, York Road, Bath Road, Clift House Road, Bedminster Down Road, the Portishead branch line and others) OpenStreetMap centrelines are used; the remaining 30% is the digitised line itself, simplified to 5m. The result stays within 13m of the digitised line over 90% of its length (22m at worst), against a printed line roughly 26m wide on the ground. Not survey-accurate; no official GIS boundary is published."}, "geometry": {"type": "Polygon", "coordinates": [[[-2.6331263, 51.4275377], [-2.6333227, 51.4275248], [-2.6333377, 51.4275243], [-2.6335864, 51.4275086], [-2.6336323, 51.427506], [-2.633909, 51.4276578], [-2.6338922, 51.4277785], [-2.6339232, 51.4278457], [-2.6339699, 51.4279948], [-2.6339735, 51.428095], [-2.634291, 51.428114], [-2.6344, 51.428364], [-2.634364, 51.429114], [-2.6343749, 51.4292708], [-2.6344872, 51.4292602], [-2.6346006, 51.4292605], [-2.6347151, 51.4292635], [-2.6348479, 51.4293087], [-2.634699, 51.4293388], [-2.6346071, 51.4293399], [-2.6344858, 51.4293337], [-2.6343529, 51.429308], [-2.634291, 51.429477], [-2.634073, 51.430841], [-2.6338, 51.430852], [-2.6334747, 51.4308512], [-2.6334748, 51.4308418], [-2.633182, 51.43083], [-2.6324, 51.430659], [-2